# tools/build.py is CRLF-mixed, so these patches' CONTEXT/ADDED lines
# legitimately end with a literal CR before the patch's own newline.  Under the
# repo's core.autocrlf=true those `\r\n` sequences are normalised away on `git
# add`, and the committed blob NO LONGER APPLIES (measured on branch_retarget:
# 6062 -> 5948 bytes, `git apply` -> "patch does not apply").  Store verbatim.
branch_retarget.patch -text
sim_text_moves.patch  -text
# byte snapshot of tools/build.py taken before the sim_text_moves hunk, kept so
# the fix can be reverted byte-exactly; must not be line-ending-normalised.
bak_build.py.prefix   -text
